A. Commit message:
gtp: Suppress list corruption splat in gtp_net_exit_batch_rtnl()

B. Change summary:
Removed the for_each_netdev() loop from gtp_net_exit_batch_rtnl() to prevent calling gtp_dellink() multiple times on the same device, which can cause list corruption. Delegated the destruction of devices to default_device_exit_batch().

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/drivers/net/gtp.c b/drivers/net/gtp.c
index d64740bf44ed3..b7b46c5e6399a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/gtp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/gtp.c
@@ -2481,11 +2481,6 @@ static void __net_exit gtp_net_exit_batch_rtnl(struct list_head *net_list,
 	list_for_each_entry(net, net_list, exit_list) {
 		struct gtp_net *gn = net_generic(net, gtp_net_id);
 		struct gtp_dev *gtp, *gtp_next;
-		struct net_device *dev;
-
-		for_each_netdev(net, dev)
-			if (dev->rtnl_link_ops == &gtp_link_ops)
-				gtp_dellink(dev, dev_to_kill);
 
 		list_for_each_entry_safe(gtp, gtp_next, &gn->gtp_dev_list, list)
 			gtp_dellink(gtp->dev, dev_to_kill);
```